>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_looper`

``` hol4
simpLib.del_looper : string -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a named tactic looper from a simpset.

A call to `del_looper name ss` returns a new simpset without the looper
whose registration name is exactly `name`.  Other loopers retain their
relative order.  If a looper with that name is subsequently added again,
it is new at that point and is appended after the remaining loopers.

The removal is recorded as a simpset strategy update, so it is preserved
when later operations rebuild the simpset from its fragment history.
The operation does not remove rewrite rules, solvers, or a simpset
fragment merely because one of them has the same name.

For a temporary alternative, placing `Excl name` in a simplification
tactic's theorem list suppresses the matching looper for that invocation
only.  This is often preferable when the looper should remain available
in the reusable simpset.

Loopers run only after rewriting and final solving have failed.  The
first applicable looper is used, and simplification restarts on all of
its subgoals.  The simpset bound set by `simpLib.limit` caps successful
looper rounds across the whole tactic invocation.  Removing a looper
therefore also removes its participation in this ordered, bounded loop.

This operation affects tactic simplification only.  Loopers do not cross
into `SIMP_CONV`, `SIMP_PROVE`, `SIMP_RULE`, or `ASM_SIMP_RULE`, whether
or not they are present in the simpset.

### Failure

If no looper has the given name, `del_looper` issues a HOL warning and
returns the original simpset unchanged.  It does not raise an exception
for that case.

### Example

``` hol4
val with_split =
  simpLib.add_looper
    ("split conjunctions", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
    simpLib.empty_ss

val without_split =
  simpLib.del_looper "split conjunctions" with_split
```

